      "dateCreated": "2026-09-28",
      "description": "AptaSelect identifies high-frequency aptamer candidate sequences from paired-end SELEX FASTQ files. Each read (R1 and R2 separately) is filtered in three stages: approximate (edit-distance) matching of both constant regions on either strand, exact-marker flanking extraction, and exact-stem random-region extraction at a user-set length. Identical sequences at every stage are counted and stably ranked by frequency. All library-design sequences, tolerances and lengths are configurable. Baseline single-process, pure-Python implementation.",
